# A user's own configs/ — scaffolded by ci-setup, holds real API keys. The whole
# directory, with a leading slash:
#
# * Anchored. A bare `configs/` matches a directory of that name at any depth,
#   so git would ignore every packaged config under packages/*/src/*/configs/,
#   and hatchling — which matches these lines relative to each package
#   directory (pypa/hatch#304) — would drop them from the wheel and the sdist.
#   Measured 2026-09-30 with hatchling's own build: a bare `configs/` empties
#   configs/ in all three wheels and all three sdists, and git then ignores
#   all 12 tracked files under packages/*/src/*/configs/.
# * The directory, not the old `configs/*.yaml`, which reached only its top
#   level. A second copy of a filled-in config one level down,
#   configs/backup/user.yaml, was not ignored; nor was configs/examples/*.yaml.
#
# Seven `!configs/<name>` negations sat here until 2026-09-30, from when these
# files lived in a repo-root configs/ and had to be un-ignored to be tracked.
# 3ae33d4 (2026-06-24) moved them into the packages, which an anchored line
# never reaches, so each named a path nothing creates: ci-setup and
# docs/CONFIGURATION.md both copy an example and rename it. `!configs/examples/`
# never un-ignored anything even then, since `configs/*.yaml` does not cross a
# slash. test_gitignore_configs.py holds both halves.
/configs/
pipeline_history/
pipeline_out.txt
# Cached provider model listings (live_model_check / ci-discover). Derived data
# with a TTL — regenerated on demand, never worth committing.
.cache/
# Private article drafts and handoffs. Deliberately no leading path: git anchors
# a line that has one to the repo root, and hatchling matches it against each
# package's directory instead (pypa/hatch#304). The old
# `handoff_templates/dc-environment*.md` therefore never matched the templates'
# new home under packages/. Bare, this matches at any depth in both, and still
# covers the repo-root handoff_templates/ where the real drafts sit.
dc-environment*.md
# The whole repo-root handoff_templates/ is a working directory for private drafts
# and handoffs, and none of it is source. Anchored with a leading slash on purpose:
# a bare line would also match the packaged templates under packages/. Hatchling
# reads an anchored line relative to each package directory, where no
# handoff_templates/ sits at the top, so the build is unaffected (pinned in
# test_gitignore_private_drafts.py).
/handoff_templates/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
*.pfx
*.p12
credentials*.json
secrets.*
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
# ci-style-profile (formerly voice-profile-bootstrap) runtime output + local config
packages/ci-style-profile/src/ci_style_profile/sources.yaml
packages/ci-style-profile/src/ci_style_profile/staging/
packages/ci-style-profile/src/ci_style_profile/profiles/

# uv
.uv/
.venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
.coverage
htmlcov/
